course: dictionary
lesson: 3528
title: Fearful and its meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The context, the words and sentences around the word, tells you which meaning is right. «In its first few months a puppy should meet many people, animals, sounds and things in a calm way» is a clue: the sentence is about pets and how they feel, so fearful must be about feeling.
explain: «A dog that met few things when young may be fearful later.» Fearful here means afraid or worried that something bad will happen. Try it: "a dog that met few things may be afraid later" still makes sense, so the meaning fits.
explain: Other meanings are older. «A fearful mess» means a very great or very bad mess, and this sense is informal and old. In old books and the Bible, fearful can mean frightening or terrible. Everyday speakers say afraid or scared more often, so use those words when you write.
fact: Fearful means afraid or worried that something bad will happen.
fact: Fearful can also mean frightening or terrible, but this meaning is old-fashioned.
fact: In «a fearful mess», fearful means very great or very bad. This is an informal, old use.
fact: In a story, «a fearful look» shows that a character is scared or worried.
fact: Good phrases to use are «fearful of» and «fearful that», as in «fearful of the dark» and «fearful that it will rain».
exercise: «A dog that met few things when young may be fearful later.» What does fearful mean here? | Very tidy and clean | Happy and full of fun | *Afraid or worried | Tall and thin
exercise: «She gave him a fearful look as the thunder crashed.» What feeling does the look show? | Joy at a party | Anger about a broken toy | Boredom in class | *Fear or worry
exercise: «The kitchen was in a fearful mess.» Find and copy one word that means very great or very bad. | *fearful | kitchen | was | mess
test: «Mia was fearful of the dark, so she left the landing light on.» What does fearful mean here? | Tidy and calm | Very quick | Dark and gloomy | *Afraid
test: Which phrase uses fearful correctly, as in the examples? | fearful fast the run | fearfully sleeping cat | *fearful that it will rain | fearful the red bike
exam: Ben says fearful always means "scary monster". Which sentence shows the right way to check his idea? | Ask a friend to guess the meaning without reading the sentence | Look only at the first word of the sentence | Count the letters in fearful and check the number | *Put "afraid" or "worried" into the sentence and see if it still makes sense
